{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep all that… in order that you may be strong.</b> The intention of this is to negate the thought of those who would refrain from the study of Torah because of the war for the land, which requires strength — and the Torah is called תּוּשִׁיָּה (Sanhedrin 26a). Therefore He said ״וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם אֶת כָּל הַמִּצְוָה״, and I have already written above that the phrase ״כָּל הַמִּצְוָה״ refers to engagement in Torah, and He designated for it a keeping, to establish a prohibition against neglecting it, and He concluded by saying <b>לְמַעַן תֶּחֶזְקוּ</b> — meaning, that on the contrary, it gives him strength and might to be strong in the war of HaShem, and so it says (Proverbs 8:14): ״אֲנִי בִינָה לִי גְבוּרָה״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:28.116694348Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}